fix(signing): pin the author's display name, not only the address (#263)

The I6 author gate admitted a commit by address alone. AuthorPolicy.Operators
was a list of addresses and CheckAuthor took an email; the display name beside
it is free text in the commit object and was compared to nothing. A real name
reached four merge commits on origin/main under a gate that was green the whole
time. The record is append-only, so this is preventable and not repairable.

An Operator is a pair now — address and the display name pinned to it — and
CheckIdentity asks both halves. internal/signing owns the rule;
scripts/no-personal-identity.sh consumes it, in the same `Name <address>`
syntax and from the same untracked list, because it is POSIX sh and cannot
call Go. A listed operator with no pinned name is refused rather than admitted.

Neither refusal echoes the name it stopped, or the one it expected: both land
in a log as public as the repository. The selftest's own leak check was itself
a denylist carrying a fragment of a real address, and its "a permitted identity
passes" fixture carried a real display name; both are invented now.

Driven by SIG-012 (an admitted address under a differing display name is
refused, and the name is absent from the output) and GH-005 (the gate fails
closed with no configuration, publishes no name, and agrees with the Go policy
on every identity both can judge). SIG-009 was already taken in code by
internal/signing/sigstoreretry_test.go, as were SIG-010 and SIG-011.

Both were observed failing first: SIG-012 on an absent CheckIdentity, GH-005 on
an absent ParseOperators, and the tracked-file sweep was driven red by planting
a permitted name in a tracked file before being made green.

